WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:05.920
We are very quickly seeing a sort of fork in&nbsp;
the Republican Party where some Republicans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:10.000
are doubling down on Trump, people like&nbsp;
Lindsey Graham, who says he's headed down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:14.640
to play golf with Trump in the next week. Kevin&nbsp;
McCarthy, who we just spoke about, who, despite a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:20.800
angry phone confrontation with Trump on January&nbsp;
6th, flew down to Florida to recruit Trump's help&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:27.200
in winning the house back in twenty. You've got&nbsp;
those people, but then you have other Republicans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:34.160
who are sometimes overtly, sometimes a little&nbsp;
more covertly distancing from Donald Trump. Mitch&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:41.040
McConnell was an incredible example of this in his&nbsp;
speech moments after the acquittal of Donald Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:46.080
in his second impeachment trial this weekend,&nbsp;
which we already discussed. Another interesting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:52.560
one is Republican Nikki Haley. Haley was the&nbsp;
governor of South Carolina. She later was Donald&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:58.480
Trump's ambassador to the United Nations. She's&nbsp;
completely abandoning Donald Trump now. And she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:04.320
says Trump, quote, let us down and that we, quote,&nbsp;
shouldn't have followed him. This is arguably&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:10.400
the most direct and forceful rebuke of Trump from&nbsp;
strictly political figures that worked for Trump.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:15.040
We've seen lots of rebukes from secretaries and&nbsp;
folks who had more concrete roles. Trump's former&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:21.920
secretary of state. Trump's former secretary of&nbsp;
defense, Trump's former national security adviser,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:27.200
John Bolton, but this is different when it's&nbsp;
Nikki Haley. Nikki Haley's interview with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:31.840
Politico was published going into this weekend,&nbsp;
and it's quite stunning. She pulls no punches.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:36.080
Let's look at some quotes. Some of these are from&nbsp;
different parts of the interview. She says, quote,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:41.200
He's not going to run for federal office again.&nbsp;
I don't think he's going to be in the picture. I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:47.360
don't think he can. He's fallen so far. She&nbsp;
says we need to acknowledge he let us down.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:51.440
He went down a path he shouldn't have and we&nbsp;
shouldn't have followed him and we shouldn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:58.000
have listened to him. And we can't let that ever&nbsp;
happen again. When I tell you I'm angry, it's an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:03.760
understatement. Mike Pence has been nothing but&nbsp;
loyal to that man. He's been nothing but a good&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:08.880
friend of that man. I am so disappointed in the&nbsp;
fact that despite the loyalty and friendship he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:14.880
had with Mike Pence, that he would do that to&nbsp;
him like I'm disgusted by it. And lastly, Nikki&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:19.600
Haley saying I think he's going to find himself&nbsp;
further and further isolated. I think his business&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:25.200
is suffering at this point. I think he's lost any&nbsp;
sort of political viability he was going to have.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:29.760
I think he's lost his social media, which meant&nbsp;
the world to him. I mean, I think he's lost the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:37.200
things that really could have kept him moving.&nbsp;
Now I want to repeat once again. This is really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:44.320
important about our analysis of what Nikki Haley&nbsp;
and others have been saying, these quotes aren't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:51.840
about realizing Nikki Haley. She gets it now.
She gets she really gets it. Not at all. These&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:59.920
people are responsible for Trump in various ways.&nbsp;
First of all, in general, Republicans for decades&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:05.440
radicalize the party more and more so that Trump&nbsp;
was then able to run and win in 2016, never would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:10.560
have been able to win a Democratic primary. But&nbsp;
they also worked for him despite knowing this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:17.280
and this has always been Trump. Nikki went and&nbsp;
was ambassador to the United Nations for Trump,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:21.840
despite all the things we knew about Trump.&nbsp;
So this is not an analysis of people having&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:27.120
an awakening and all of that stuff. And these&nbsp;
are good Republicans. This is a story about a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:33.280
Republican Party that is currently pulling itself&nbsp;
apart or maybe is going to pull itself apart. Some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:39.280
newcomers are riding the Trump wave, Marjorie&nbsp;
Taylor Greene, Lauren Bobert, Madison, Cawthorn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:46.240
and others. Some long timers are just sticking&nbsp;
with Trump. Like Lindsey Graham. Some long timers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:50.240
seem to be distancing from Trump&nbsp;
like Mitch McConnell and others.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:55.280
And then you've got people that were never really&nbsp;
with Trump, Mitt Romney. He thought maybe he could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.280 --> 00:04:01.120
be Trump's secretary of state. He went and had&nbsp;
turtle soup and frogs legs with Trump early on,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:07.920
but has basically a distance from Trump years&nbsp;
and years ago. Nikki Haley wants a continued&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:12.800
political career. She's young. She's only forty&nbsp;
nine compared to some of these guys in their 70s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:20.800
and 80s. She wants to wash herself of the stink&nbsp;
of Trump. So now she's going through this process.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:28.960
And what we're learning here is quite simply,&nbsp;
they knew all along what Trump was. They merely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:36.640
pretended not to know when Trump was their&nbsp;
ride to notoriety or a position of power&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.640 --> 00:04:42.400
or a position of prestige. They are even&nbsp;
more immoral than we thought because they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:47.760
weren't even tricked by Trump. If they were&nbsp;
really tricked, we could say they're dumb,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:54.080
but they're less immoral. They weren't tricked.&nbsp;
They looked away deliberately. They knew all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:59.920
along what it was. And they want I mean, look at&nbsp;
Chris Christie. Remember Chris Christie denouncing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:06.320
Trump endlessly during the primary in which he&nbsp;
ran and Lindsey Graham, too, by the way, then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:11.440
standing behind Trump, figuratively and literally.&nbsp;
Remember the video of Chris Christie standing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.440 --> 00:05:17.600
behind Trump looking like he ate a bad oyster&nbsp;
and saying, yeah, Trump, Trump, I'm with Trump.&nbsp;

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:22.480
And then eventually Chris Christie starting&nbsp;
to make a little more sense on Trump over the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.480 --> 00:05:28.560
last six months or so. He knew all along it was&nbsp;
just a calculation. How much power can I grab&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:34.880
by attaching myself to what was then the&nbsp;
rising star of Trump? They all knew all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:39.680
along. And none of them deserve to be forgiven.&nbsp;
But from a practical perspective, it does raise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.680 --> 00:05:43.600
questions about the future of the Republican&nbsp;
Party, which we will continue to talk about.

